{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016ozaa4t45sP4XUR4hX5pL3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is in order and committed. Session complete with ~35 min of buffer.\n\n## Summary\n\n**New best val_loss = `3.7967`** (down from the prior session's 3.8041; baseline 4.1955), robustly confirmed across **3 clean single-GPU runs** {3.7967, 3.7975, 3.8014}, mean 3.7985.\n\n### The win this session: model **width**\nThe prior session had swept batch and depth but never width. At fixed depth=6 / bs128, sweeping `n_embd`:\n\n| n_embd | step_avg | steps | val_loss |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 512 | 112ms | 2686 | 3.8108 |\n| **640** | 141ms | 2126 | **3.7967 ← BEST** |\n| 768 (prev) | 172ms | 1753 | 3.8041 |\n| 1024 | 245ms | ~1250 | lost (killed) |\n\nWidth is U-shaped with the optimum at **n_embd=640**: narrowing 768→640 buys +22% optimizer steps while keeping enough capacity that the warmdown is just as effective. Same capacity↔throughput tradeoff as depth/batch, now on the width axis.\n\n### Everything else around the optimum was flat or negative\nDepth 6→7 (tie), warmdown 0.28→0.40 (tie), Muon LR 2× (tie); and clear losses from batch→64, MLP 3×, head_dim 64, logit soft-cap, untied embeddings, and width 1024. That cluster of ties/losses is the signature of a well-optimized point — the config is now balanced on every axis.\n\n### Deliverables (all committed on `claude-code-autonomous`)\n- `exp/best.py` — 6L, n_embd=640, n_head=5, bs128. One-command repro:\n  `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 torchrun --standalone --nproc_per_node=1 exp/best.py`\n- `logs/best.out` — proof of 3.7967\n- `REPORT.md` — full narrative + 3 plots (`img/trajectories.png`, `img/width_sweep.png`, `img/final_bar.png`)\n- `RESULTS.md` — complete experiment table including all negatives"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":823,"cache_read_input_tokens":108088,