{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0198Mdy6499FgadKC7mtjxMT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Everything committed with a clean tree and ~23 min of safe buffer.\n\n## Final status\n\n**Best val_loss = `3.7967`** (`exp/best.py`: 6 layers, n_embd=640, n_head=5, batch=128) — verified across 3 clean single-GPU runs {3.7967, 3.7975, 3.8014}, mean **3.7985**. Beats the prior session's 3.8041 and the 4.1955 baseline.\n\nThis session's contribution: I swept the one major axis the prior run missed — **model width** — and found a real win at **n_embd=640** (the prior used 768). Then I confirmed the config is at a true optimum by failing to beat it on every other lever:\n\n- **Wins:** width 768→640 (−0.007, robust mid-run gap of ~0.024)\n- **Ties (noise floor):** depth 6↔7, warmdown 0.28↔0.40, LR 3.6e-3↔4.7e-3, Muon LR 2×\n- **Losses:** width 512 & 1024, batch 64, MLP 3×, head_dim 64, Muon momentum 0.90 & 0.98, logit soft-cap, untied embeddings\n\nThe unifying principle across both sessions holds: in a fixed 5-min, undertrained budget, **trade capacity for throughput up to the point where the warmdown can still exploit the model's capacity** — width=640 is that sweet spot on the width axis.\n\nDeliverables all current and committed on `claude-code-autonomous`: `exp/best.py` (+ one-command repro), `logs/best.out` (proof), `REPORT.md` (narrative + 3 plots), `RESULTS.md` (full table incl. all negatives)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":377,"cache_read_input_tokens":116970,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":377},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82495903-e006-464b-90dc-5af01f7557e1","uuid":"f067bd82-9001-42fd-adee-deb42377be24","request_id":"req_011Cbiy9x